      "writtenOn": "2021-07-12T21:21:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need the date field? Since the field allocated for cros_fwid is 32 bytes, we can\u0027t use a long board name and we can\u0027t use the sub-minor version.\n\nI think the date field is redundant. How about the following?\n\n  * board_name: 16\n  * _: 1\n  * major: 6\n  * .: 1\n  * minor: 3\n  * .: 1\n  * sub-minor: 3\n  * \\0: 1\n\nThe board name field is also redundant but not always, I think because we sometimes use a fw image named baseboard for a variant.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "351b7f78de8bd3539f388b32a94065f4cb986a5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f917055_d3ee9d41",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-20T16:43:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sub-minor (aka CHROMOS_PATCH) is set to the date for non official builds. If we set this to 0 for non-official builds there will be two side effects. The fwid will not exactly match the value reported by bios and OS. It will not be immediately obvious that it\u0027s a non-official build. This can still be mostly inferred from user/hostname in the BUILD string. \n\nPossible solutions:\n* Add a dedicated field indicating if it\u0027s an official build, or append an indicator to the BUILD string, e.g. NON-OFFICIAL 2021-05-20 16:43:18.657 robbarnes@robbarnes0\n* Make the fwid field 64 bytes\n* Instead of setting sub-minor to 0, set it to something that indicates it\u0027s a non-official build, e.g. guybrush_13434.0.999 | guybrush_13434.0.loc | guybrush_13434.0.xxx",
      "parentUuid": "4b138a00_2163dcd1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "351b7f78de8bd3539f388b32a94065f4cb986a5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5f5e059_10f4653d",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-20T20:26:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... I think 64 (for RO) + 64 (for RW) are too much for smaller ROMs. \n\nWhat does non-official build exactly mean in our context? Do the major and minor mean anything for non-official builds? I\u0027m wondering if we can omit major and minor (e.g. guybrush_2021_05_20_163) for non-official builds.\n\nUsing a marker also sounds reasonable to me. (e.g. \u00279999\u0027 to mimic what ebuilds do). \n\nFYI: We use \u0027+\u0027 to mark a dirty build (e.g. guybrush_v2.0.8770+f47439f75 v.s. guybrush_v2.0.8770-f47439f75). It means the image includes a local change.",
      "parentUuid": "3f917055_d3ee9d41",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "351b7f78de8bd3539f388b32a94065f4cb986a5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97d88e10_51eee376",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 19,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-21T18:31:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The build_release recipe sets the CHROMEOS_OFFICIAL flag: https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:infra/recipes/recipes/build_release.py;l\u003d39. For non-official builds, major and minor version is still useful. It will match the version of the last repo sync (specifically, the last time https://source.corp.google.com/chromeos_public/src/third_party/chromiumos-overlay/chromeos/config/chromeos_version.sh?q\u003dCHROMEOS_VERSION.sh was synced). So you get a hint of what a non-official build is based on. Sub-minor (CHROMEOS_PATCH) does not matter for non-official builds AFAICT.\n\nSince + is already in the ec build version, I don\u0027t think it needs to be indicated in the fwid too. \n\nHow about removing the year, i.e. guybrush_13983.0.05_20_1631? There\u0027s still risk of truncation, but it\u0027s much less likely.",
      "parentUuid": "c5f5e059_10f4653d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "351b7f78de8bd3539f388b32a94065f4cb986a5a",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
